Subject: [PATCH] steps: skip the Yosys log line ahead of the JSON in stat.json

Since 3.1.0.dev4, Yosys.Synthesis hands the PDK's Liberty files to Yosys as
they are, instead of the uncompressed copies remove_cells_from_lib() wrote up to
3.1.0.dev3. With a PDK whose LIB points at .lib.gz, every `stat -liberty`
logs

    Found gzip magic in file `....lib.gz', decompressing using zlib.

and `tee -o` captures that line into reports/stat.json ahead of the JSON. The
step then dies with

    json.decoder.JSONDecodeError: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)

right after synthesis, in every PDK of the image.

Not reported upstream yet, librelane main reads stat.json the same way.
Against librelane 3.1.0.dev4. Drop this once the pinned release carries a fix.
---
--- librelane/steps/pyosys.py
+++ librelane/steps/pyosys.py
@@ -623,6 +623,11 @@
 
         stats_file = os.path.join(self.step_dir, "reports", "stat.json")
         stats_str = open(stats_file).read()
+        # Yosys log()s "Found gzip magic in file ..." whenever stat -liberty
+        # reads a .lib.gz, and tee -o writes that line into stat.json ahead of
+        # the JSON. Skip to the JSON object, index() still fails loudly if
+        # there is none.
+        stats_str = stats_str[stats_str.index("{"):]
         stats = json.loads(stats_str, parse_float=Decimal)
 
         metric_updates["design__instance__count"] = stats["design"]["num_cells"]
